# Slow: repeated wood decode per stain; polygon Paths and edge Stroke during board recording.
# Why: brushes/shaders are already cached, but source decode and temporary geometry are not.
# Expected win: one source decode instead of N; reusable polygon path and outline stroke.
# Risk: scratch path requires synchronous, non-reentrant render-thread use. Vertex lists remain.
# Still-layer caching already limits this cost to board re-records, not every sea frame.
diff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/mauro/wgbg/WoodPieces.kt b/app/src/main/java/com/mauro/wgbg/WoodPieces.kt
index cf72b91..a981f4f 100644
